-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
DEV KEY ONLY — NEVER USE FOR PRODUCTION RELEASES.

This file holds the Ed25519 public key used for CI smoke-test signing of
appcast entries on non-tagged workflow runs. The matching private key lives
ONLY in the GH Actions secret AUTOUPDATE_ED25519_PRIVATE_KEY_DEV and is
regenerated freely — losing it has zero blast radius because no shipped
binary embeds this key.

Production releases (tagged v1.7.0+) use AUTOUPDATE_ED25519_PUBLIC_KEY (and
its matching private key in 1Password org-vault BALL/Auto-Update/Ed25519-Private)
— see .planning/phases/999.8-auto-update-sparkle-winsparkle/ED25519-KEY-RUNBOOK.md.

When regenerating the dev keypair, run on any machine with the Sparkle
tools (or openssl):

  openssl genpkey -algorithm ED25519 -out dev-private.pem
  openssl pkey -in dev-private.pem -pubout -out dev-public.pem

Then paste dev-public.pem's contents into THIS file (replacing this header
block) and update AUTOUPDATE_ED25519_PRIVATE_KEY_DEV in GH Actions secrets.

The placeholder below is intentionally INVALID — CI smoke-test path treats
a placeholder pubkey as "skip Ed25519 verification" so the unsigned-fallback
build path works without a real dev key procured.

INVALID_DEV_PLACEHOLDER_REGENERATE_BEFORE_FIRST_CI_SMOKE_RUN
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
